WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Scene reading begins with orientation.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.948
Identify image direction, scale, date, time, sensor, and location confidence.

00:00:07.948 --> 00:00:12.584
Locate stable reference features before examining change or movement.

00:00:12.584 --> 00:00:18.987
Without orientation, a plausible interpretation may belong to the wrong place or direction.

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:26.714
Visible features may include roads, paths, buildings, vehicles, terrain, vegetation, water, construction, access routes, and hazards.

00:00:26.714 --> 00:00:33.116
Describe shape, position, count, condition, and relationship using neutral language before assigning meaning.

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:40.402
Movement patterns can be observed in video or repeated frames, but they rarely establish motive.

00:00:40.402 --> 00:00:46.363
A stopped vehicle, gathered people, or changed route may have many explanations.

00:00:46.363 --> 00:00:50.116
Report the visible behavior and preserve alternatives.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:54.752
Shadows, roofs, trees, terrain, and perspective can hide features.

00:00:54.752 --> 00:01:00.271
Distance can compress space, while oblique angles can make objects overlap.

00:01:00.271 --> 00:01:06.674
Seasonal vegetation and temporary materials can change appearance without indicating a meaningful event.

00:01:06.674 --> 00:01:09.102
Separate observation from interpretation.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:15.063
An observation might be that water covers a marked section of road.

00:01:15.063 --> 00:01:19.700
An interpretation may be that the route is impassable.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:27.427
The second judgment may require depth, vehicle, ground, or official information not visible in the image.

00:01:27.427 --> 00:01:30.738
Use annotations and evidence references carefully.

00:01:30.738 --> 00:01:39.349
Mark the exact source frame and location, avoid covering important pixels, and distinguish confirmed features from tentative identifications.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.102
Honest limits make the observation more useful.
